# Instrument fail-able host code

**Moral:** Write the span with the feature. Job counts and leaf CLI traces are not enough to tell why and when a host loop failed.

LLM hops: skill `golang-quality` C15. Process Olly: `internal/cli/telemetry.go`. Leaf CLI: `internal/pimalaya/runner.go`. Report seats: `internal/mailreport/trace.go`.

**CONSTRAINT:** New or changed host Go that can fail, hang, or call outbound (HTTP, Himalaya/Neverest, SQLite apply, IMAP bind) MUST start an OpenTelemetry span on that orchestration, with attributes that name the work and the ids needed to explain a miss.

- MUST: `otel.Tracer("github.com/xynova/should-i-read/internal/<pkg>")`, `tracer.Start`, `defer span.End()`
- MUST: attributes for why/when (job id, object hash, folder, envelope id, status, model)
- MUST: `span.RecordError(err)` and `span.SetStatus(codes.Error, ...)` on failure; named-return defers use `err =`
- MUST NOT: ship a new fail-able loop with only a count, SQLite error column, or `tmp/delete-job-*.json`
- MUST NOT: treat `pimalaya.RunJSON` or Polypus HTTP traces as the only span for a host job
- NEVER: defer spans to a later cleanup PR

Enforcement: planned `.go` diffs; grep `tracer.Start` / `otel.Tracer` on new orchestration; checklist below
Violation: STOP, add the span (or turn Olly on for that command), re-verify

Before writing a new or changed function, complete this gate in working memory:

```text
Candidate: [function or loop]
Can fail, hang, or call outbound: YES: [quote] / NO
Already starts a span (or is a child that already carries the failure ids): YES: [quote] / NO
Decision: ADD SPAN | KEEP | SKIP
```

IF YES and NO → ADD SPAN. SKIP only for pure helpers, formatters, or `*_test.go` that do not assert telemetry.

CORRECT:
```go
ctx, span := tracer.Start(ctx, "maildelete.ApplyJob",
    trace.WithAttributes(
        attribute.String("delete.job_id", jobID),
        attribute.String("delete.folder", folder),
        attribute.String("delete.envelope_id", env),
        attribute.String("delete.object_hash", it.ObjectHash),
    ),
)
defer span.End()
```

PROHIBITED:
```go
// maildelete apply calls Himalaya; only pimalaya.RunJSON is spanned.
// Cart shows "failed 41 / trashed 0" with no host span attributes.
```

**CONSTRAINT:** While developing a command that can fail, Olly MUST stay on for that command.

- MUST: keep `startTelemetry` for `mail overview serve`, cart apply, and other jobs under debug
- MUST NOT: add that command to `skipTelemetryForCmd` to make the loop "fast"
- MUST NOT: treat overview.js overlay as the observability plan

Enforcement: `skipTelemetryForCmd` vs the command being changed; Olly dump dir `logs/failures`
Violation: STOP, remove the skip (or add a debug override), re-verify

CORRECT:
```text
Developing cart apply on overview serve → Olly starts; host apply span exports.
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
skipTelemetryForCmd returns true for overview serve while delete jobs fail closed.
```

## Pre-change checklist

- [ ] **Host span on the new loop:** Orchestration that can fail starts `tracer.Start`
      Method: grep the new package for `tracer.Start` (not only `pimalaya.RunJSON`)
      Pass: span name plus why/when attributes
      Fail: STOP, add the span
- [ ] **Olly not skipped:** The command under development still calls `startTelemetry`
      Method: read `skipTelemetryForCmd` for that leaf
      Pass: skip is false, or a documented non-fail-able command
      Fail: STOP, keep Olly on
